      sources: "Sources: examples/provider-notices (Invoke-PnRoute, Test-PnTaskPayload, Invoke-PnEvidence). Chapter 08, Steps 1.4–1.5.",
      say: `Step 1.4 routes the full collection with the agency's own routing file, as a dry run. The service desk reads the payloads before anything is sent. Expected: payloads written, nothing sent; every security advisory and retirement has one, and each assignment group is one the change manager recognizes. Step 1.5 is the smoke test: four checks, each with its expected result written down before you run it. Every provider read; a second routing writes nothing new; every payload valid; and the evidence chain clean. On the fixtures, the first routing created eight tasks and the second created none.`,
      detail: `Step 1.4, route as a dry run, and read the payloads (G6): route the full collection with the agency's routing, and have the service desk read the payloads before anything is sent. ./Invoke-PnCollect.ps1 -SettingsPath <settings-file> -OutputPath "$out/stage/all"; ./Invoke-PnRoute.ps1 -NoticesPath "$out/stage/all/notices.json" -RoutingPath $s.routing.path -StatePath "$out/state.json" -OutputPath "$out/stage/route"; ./Invoke-PnEvidence.ps1 -EvidencePath $ev -RunPath "$out/stage/route" -ChangeRecord $s.changeRecord. Expected: Dry run: N payloads written to .../tasks, nothing sent. Every security advisory and retirement has a payload; each payload's assignment group is one the change manager recognizes. Supports SI-5 c, d; CM-3 b, f; CM-4; CP-2 e: every notice that needs action has a task with an owner; retirements and maintenance ask for a plan review; KSI-SCR-MON, KSI-CMT-LMC, KSI-CMT-RVP, KSI-RPL-ARP; evidence stage/route/ (tasks/, routing.csv, state.json) and its record. Step 1.5, smoke test (G1 to G7): four checks, each with its expected result written before you run it; the smoke test uses its own state file, so it doesn't touch the stage's routing state. Design guidance. ST-01 the collection read every enabled provider; ST-02 a second routing of the same collection writes no payload; ST-03 every payload passes Test-PnTaskPayload; ST-04 the evidence chain checks clean. Commands: collect to "$out/smoke/collect"; print 'ST-01 providers read: ' with the providers' keys; route twice to "$out/smoke/route1" and "$out/smoke/route2" with -StatePath "$out/smoke/state.json"; count invalid payloads with Test-PnTaskPayload; record the collection; ./Invoke-PnEvidence.ps1 -EvidencePath $ev -Check. Expected: ST-01 lists every enabled provider; the second routing prints Payloads: 0 create, 0 update, 0 close; ST-03 invalid payloads: 0; SUMS Pass and CHAIN Pass. Dry run, November 9, 2026, on the test fixture: ST-01 providers read: azure, m365, oci, the first routing 8 create, the second 0 create, 0 update, 0 close, and ST-03 invalid payloads: 0. Supports CA-7; SI-5; KSI-MLA-EVC, KSI-SCR-MON; evidence smoke/ and its record.`,
      cite: [],
      ref: "Stage 1 — Steps 1.4 and 1.5",
