      sources: "Sources: Chapter 08, “Checklist”; “Continue the book”; workbook index.",
      say: `Here's what done looks like. One settings file per stage, with no secrets, filed with the change record. The test pre-flight passed, and every provider was enabled and cross-checked one at a time. The smoke test passed. Both plans were approved by hash, applied and recorded in test. The test evidence passed, and the security officer and the board recorded the go/no-go. Production's pre-flight passed the seventh check, production routed as a dry run for a week before sending, and its evidence passes every week. That's the end of Building Provider Notices. Thanks for watching.`,
      detail: `Checklist: One settings file per stage, no secrets, filed with the change record. The test pre-flight passed, and every provider was enabled and cross-checked one at a time. The smoke test passed: ST-01 to ST-04. The alert plan and the rollback plan were each approved by hash, applied and recorded in test. The test stage's evidence passed, and the go/no-go was recorded by the ISSO and the change advisory board. Production's pre-flight passed PF-07. Production routed as a dry run for a week before sending was turned on. Production's evidence passes -Check -Stage production every week. Continue: previous, Chapter 07 — The Weekly Digest and Evidence; the workbook index.`,
